WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.140
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.410 --> 01:34.920
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.250 --> 01:37.720
[Episode 37]

4
01:52.590 --> 01:55.710
Comrade Han Dongshan of the 4th Front Army

5
01:55.420 --> 01:58.870
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

6
01:55.950 --> 01:57.880
is already at Dawei Town at the foot of the mountain,

7
01:57.880 --> 01:59.030
waiting for us.

8
01:59.590 --> 02:02.840
The world had no roads to begin with.

9
02:03.770 --> 02:06.050
But when enough people walk the same path,

10
02:06.050 --> 02:07.410
it becomes a road.

11
02:08.330 --> 02:09.610
We have

12
02:10.930 --> 02:15.890
trampled the great snow mountain under our feet.

13
02:18.960 --> 02:20.079
Heaven,

14
02:20.960 --> 02:21.960
earth,

15
02:22.560 --> 02:23.360
and men.

16
02:25.240 --> 02:26.290
Magnificent!

17
02:28.120 --> 02:29.560
Magnificent!

18
02:30.680 --> 02:32.730
The Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

19
02:32.730 --> 02:35.910
is the first army to conquer the great snow mountain.

20
02:33.490 --> 02:36.270
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo]

21
02:36.840 --> 02:38.329
It's unprecedented,

22
02:38.120 --> 02:39.150
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

23
02:38.400 --> 02:40.450
but there will surely be successors.

24
02:39.150 --> 02:40.190
[Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

25
02:40.890 --> 02:42.050
In the future,

26
02:42.400 --> 02:44.930
there will definitely be more and more people

27
02:44.930 --> 02:45.960
standing here,

28
02:46.870 --> 02:48.800
appreciating this magnificence.

29
02:48.950 --> 02:50.800
[Zhou Enlai, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo,]

30
02:49.560 --> 02:50.490
In the future,

31
02:50.800 --> 02:51.730
[Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

32
02:51.730 --> 02:52.660
[and Political Commissar-General of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

33
02:51.740 --> 02:52.770
they

34
02:54.170 --> 02:55.370
will also definitely

35
02:55.680 --> 02:58.030
become the masters of this country.

36
03:00.750 --> 03:02.910
[Mao Zedong, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee]

37
03:02.910 --> 03:05.070
[Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

38
03:04.610 --> 03:05.240
Changfeng.

39
03:05.240 --> 03:05.640
Here.

40
03:06.210 --> 03:07.940
Where is Changbao's notebook?

41
03:24.170 --> 03:25.170
I know

42
03:26.490 --> 03:28.840
what character Changbao wrote.

43
03:30.930 --> 03:32.090
It's "cloud".

44
03:32.770 --> 03:33.520
"Cloud"?

45
03:34.770 --> 03:35.720
Changbao!

46
03:37.290 --> 03:39.120
You were right!

47
03:39.760 --> 03:40.850
Snow

48
03:42.730 --> 03:45.820
is clouds falling from the sky!

49
03:55.560 --> 03:57.120
More than 90 years ago,

50
03:57.680 --> 03:59.079
a Tibetan guide

51
03:59.079 --> 04:00.010
named Morijian

52
04:00.400 --> 04:01.560
witnessed with his own eyes

53
04:01.560 --> 04:03.920
the heroic feat of the Red Army crossing Jiajin Mountain,

54
04:03.920 --> 04:07.010
and gladly accepted the name Ma Denghong, given to him by the Red Army

55
04:07.010 --> 04:09.370
(which he later officially adopted as his Han Chinese name).

56
04:09.370 --> 04:12.170
Ma Denghong saw many Red Army officers and soldiers

57
04:12.170 --> 04:15.310
sacrifice their lives due to the cold and altitude sickness.

58
04:15.310 --> 04:17.990
He couldn't bear to let these once vibrant lives

59
04:18.170 --> 04:20.170
stay on the freezing snow mountain,

60
04:20.750 --> 04:24.000
so he carried these fallen Red Army soldiers down the mountain.

61
04:24.000 --> 04:25.240
As the news spread,

62
04:25.390 --> 04:27.610
many Tibetan people spontaneously went up the mountain,

63
04:27.610 --> 04:29.880
along the route the Red Army took to cross the snow mountain,

64
04:29.880 --> 04:32.010
searching for the remains of the Red Army soldiers,

65
04:32.010 --> 04:34.870
and carrying them down the snow mountain one by one.

66
04:35.170 --> 04:37.680
This is the reverence of the living for life.

67
04:38.320 --> 04:40.580
This is the simplest emotion of mankind.

68
04:40.970 --> 04:42.360
The remains of these Red Army soldiers

69
04:42.360 --> 04:43.880
were buried together at the foot of the mountain,

70
04:43.880 --> 04:46.210
on a hill in the ancient village of Qiaoqi.

71
04:46.290 --> 04:47.930
To make it easier to identify later,

72
04:47.930 --> 04:51.409
the local Tibetan villagers planted a pine tree in front of the grave.

73
04:51.409 --> 04:52.050
Today,

74
04:52.050 --> 04:54.210
this pine tree has grown lush branches and leaves,

75
04:54.210 --> 04:56.100
shaped like a umbrella-shaped crown.

76
04:56.100 --> 04:57.270
The local Tibetan people

77
04:57.270 --> 04:59.510
gave it an affectionate name,

78
04:59.780 --> 05:01.170
the Red Army Umbrella.

79
05:01.360 --> 05:05.220
[Maoxian, Sichuan]

80
05:02.560 --> 05:03.320
From now on,

81
05:03.560 --> 05:06.290
the general policy of the 1st and 4th Front Armies

82
05:06.410 --> 05:09.680
should be to occupy Sichuan, Shaanxi, and Gansu provinces

83
05:09.900 --> 05:12.800
and establish a unified Soviet regime across the region.

84
05:12.800 --> 05:14.530
According to the current plan,

85
05:14.530 --> 05:16.200
the 2 armies should advance towards

86
05:16.200 --> 05:18.660
the area between the Min and Jialing rivers.

87
05:18.750 --> 05:20.140
When further advance became difficult,

88
05:19.870 --> 05:21.290
[Zhang Guotao, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo,]

89
05:20.490 --> 05:22.970
parts of Shaanxi and Gansu

90
05:21.290 --> 05:22.720
[Chairman of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission]

91
05:23.090 --> 05:25.050
would serve as strategic maneuvering areas.

92
05:25.050 --> 05:25.800
Therefore,

93
05:26.170 --> 05:27.290
firmly holding

94
05:27.560 --> 05:30.850
Maoxian, Beichuan, and Weizhou in our hands

95
05:31.240 --> 05:34.240
and defeating Hu Zongnan's southward advance

96
05:34.510 --> 05:36.630
is the pivot of this plan.

97
05:40.030 --> 05:41.440
Fight Hu Zongnan?

98
05:43.610 --> 05:45.080
Is it that easy?

99
05:45.930 --> 05:48.730
Then how should we reply to the Central Committee?

100
05:49.320 --> 05:52.090
Should we wait for Comrade Changhao's opinion?

101
06:12.200 --> 06:13.050
Report.

102
06:13.350 --> 06:16.280
Chairman Zhang, Political Commissar Chen replied.

103
06:27.410 --> 06:28.120
Look.

104
06:28.560 --> 06:29.800
Comrade Changhao's

105
06:30.050 --> 06:32.050
thoughts are consistent with mine.

106
06:33.650 --> 06:35.450
Reply to the Central Committee.

107
06:35.850 --> 06:36.880
Inform them

108
06:37.610 --> 06:39.460
that we agree with the policy of developing

109
06:39.460 --> 06:41.590
towards Sichuan, Shaanxi, and Gansu,

110
06:41.760 --> 06:43.760
but disagree with the current plan.

111
06:44.530 --> 06:46.090
The terrain around Beichuan

112
06:46.090 --> 06:48.360
is not conducive to the movement of large troops,

113
06:48.360 --> 06:50.320
and Hu Zongnan is well prepared,

114
06:50.470 --> 06:52.330
so it is not advisable to go north.

115
06:52.490 --> 06:54.170
Attacking east from the Min River

116
06:54.170 --> 06:56.030
or attacking Songpan to the north

117
06:56.050 --> 06:57.580
are both disadvantageous.

118
06:58.940 --> 07:00.250
My suggestion is

119
07:00.680 --> 07:04.440
that the 1st Front Army goes north along the Dajinchuan River

120
07:04.460 --> 07:05.340
to occupy Aba,

121
07:06.160 --> 07:08.920
while the 4th Front Army turns back south

122
07:08.640 --> 07:14.740
[Map of Shaanxi and Gansu]

123
07:09.790 --> 07:12.050
and advances to the area west of Songpan,

124
07:12.290 --> 07:15.240
avoiding the main areas ruled by the Kuomintang.

125
07:16.680 --> 07:19.850
Or we can attack south first,

126
07:20.120 --> 07:21.440
take Chengdu directly,

127
07:21.440 --> 07:23.900
reach the Yangtze River, and fight to Wuhan,

128
07:25.560 --> 07:29.320
then choose an opportunity to go north.

129
07:29.760 --> 07:31.440
These are all possible.

130
07:34.090 --> 07:34.760
All right.

131
07:34.940 --> 07:36.050
Organize it.

132
07:37.680 --> 07:39.659
Send it to the Central Committee in the names

133
07:39.659 --> 07:40.710
of Comrade Changhao and me.

134
07:40.710 --> 07:41.670
[Huang Chao, Secretary-General of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission,]

135
07:40.800 --> 07:41.330
Yes, sir.

136
07:41.670 --> 07:42.630
[Secretary-General of the Sichuan-Shaanxi Provincial Soviet Government]

137
07:59.590 --> 08:02.920
[Maogong County, Sichuan]

138
08:00.120 --> 08:01.260
Chairman Zhang, Political Commissar Chen,

139
08:01.260 --> 08:02.500
and Commander-in-Chief Xu

140
08:02.500 --> 08:04.630
ordered me to welcome you leaders here

141
08:04.680 --> 08:06.810
and the comrades of the 1st Front Army.

142
08:06.940 --> 08:08.170
Comrade Li Xiannian.

143
08:08.680 --> 08:10.120
How old are you?

144
08:09.980 --> 08:12.610
[Li Xiannian, Political Commissar of the 30th Red Army]

145
08:11.240 --> 08:13.410
I'll be 26 in a few days.

146
08:13.520 --> 08:14.490
I was born in the Year of the Rooster.

147
08:14.490 --> 08:15.680
You are from Huang'an, Hubei?

148
08:15.680 --> 08:16.360
Yes.

149
08:16.850 --> 08:17.780
How did you know?

150
08:18.050 --> 08:19.980
Your fellow countryman Dong Biwu,

151
08:20.050 --> 08:21.320
Mr. Dong, mentioned you to me.

152
08:21.320 --> 08:23.450
I just didn't expect you to be so young.

153
08:23.970 --> 08:25.300
Mr. Dong and Chen Tanqiu

154
08:25.310 --> 08:26.260
are my seniors.

155
08:26.440 --> 08:28.050
Mr. Dong is at the back of the column.

156
08:28.050 --> 08:29.320
You can see him later.

157
08:30.090 --> 08:30.970
That's great.

158
08:31.700 --> 08:32.830
Right, give it to me.

159
08:35.010 --> 08:36.700
This is from our Commander-in-Chief Xu Xiangqian,

160
08:36.700 --> 08:39.830
the letter and map he specially sent someone to deliver.

161
08:40.590 --> 08:41.140
A map?

162
08:41.250 --> 08:41.679
Yes.

163
08:42.610 --> 08:43.820
And he told me

164
08:44.130 --> 08:46.460
to hand the letter to you personally.

165
08:46.890 --> 08:48.560
This map is the best meeting gift.

166
08:48.560 --> 08:49.080
Yes.

167
08:49.100 --> 08:50.460
A map is a treasure.

168
08:50.490 --> 08:50.970
Yes.

169
09:12.680 --> 09:13.480
Comrades.

170
09:13.680 --> 09:16.000
Comrade Xiangqian gave a very detailed account

171
09:16.000 --> 09:17.530
in his letter of the enemy's deployment

172
09:17.530 --> 09:19.250
and the situation

173
09:19.770 --> 09:21.250
of the 4th Front Army.

174
09:21.680 --> 09:22.930
The letter also mentioned

175
09:22.930 --> 09:25.020
that the Central Red Army came from afar

176
09:25.020 --> 09:28.190
and must rest and replenish as soon as possible.

177
09:28.560 --> 09:32.040
The 4th Front Army will wipe out the enemy in front.

178
09:32.600 --> 09:34.840
Such sincerity is touching.

179
09:35.010 --> 09:36.720
This is what revolutionary comrades are,

180
09:36.720 --> 09:38.600
showing utter devotion to each other.

181
09:38.600 --> 09:40.320
We would like to thank the comrades of the 4th Front Army.

182
09:40.320 --> 09:40.890
It's our duty.

183
09:40.890 --> 09:42.600
Leaders, please follow me into the city.

184
09:42.600 --> 09:43.080
Okay.

185
09:43.290 --> 09:43.890
Let's go.

186
09:44.320 --> 09:44.930
Let's go.

187
10:35.770 --> 10:36.630
Young comrade.

188
10:36.640 --> 10:37.900
Here's a quilt for you.

189
10:38.290 --> 10:39.180
Thank you, comrade.

190
10:39.180 --> 10:40.110
You're welcome.

191
10:43.620 --> 10:44.930
Freshly boiled salt.

192
10:45.430 --> 10:45.980
Here.

193
10:47.270 --> 10:48.150
Take it.

194
10:49.560 --> 10:50.840
You haven't got any salt yet, right?

195
10:50.840 --> 10:52.200
Here, take it.

196
10:52.480 --> 10:53.440
Welcome.

197
10:53.660 --> 10:55.120
Come back if you need more.

198
10:55.170 --> 10:55.760
Okay.

199
10:56.250 --> 10:57.250
Freshly boiled salt.

200
10:57.250 --> 10:58.900
We boiled it ourselves. Take it.

201
10:58.900 --> 11:00.140
Freshly boiled.

202
11:00.680 --> 11:01.560
Fine salt!

203
11:01.580 --> 11:02.300
Take it.

204
11:04.410 --> 11:07.710
[Zhang Side, Soldier of the 4th Front Army]

205
11:05.080 --> 11:05.870
Comrade.

206
11:06.480 --> 11:08.370
Come, take a bag of salt.

207
11:10.010 --> 11:11.140
Thank you, comrade.

208
11:11.150 --> 11:12.080
You're welcome.

209
11:13.440 --> 11:15.800
How is this salt boiled?

210
11:17.050 --> 11:19.110
Here, there is a special kind of stone.

211
11:19.110 --> 11:20.430
Put the stone in a pot and boil it.

212
11:20.430 --> 11:22.030
Boil out the water and dry it,

213
11:22.080 --> 11:23.070
and it becomes salt.

214
11:23.070 --> 11:25.000
How many stones do you have to boil?

215
11:25.150 --> 11:26.610
For this small bag of salt,

216
11:26.690 --> 11:28.760
it takes about 5 or 6 carts of stones.

217
11:29.720 --> 11:31.360
That's not easy at all.

218
11:31.740 --> 11:32.740
I can't take this.

219
11:33.890 --> 11:35.010
Take it. Don't be polite.

220
11:35.010 --> 11:36.670
This bag of salt is specially boiled for you,

221
11:36.670 --> 11:38.060
the big brothers of the 1st Front Army.

222
11:38.060 --> 11:38.660
Take it.

223
11:38.730 --> 11:40.460
You just called me big brother?

224
11:40.830 --> 11:42.630
But I should be younger than you.

225
11:43.660 --> 11:45.360
Our Political Commissar Li Xiannian said,

226
11:45.360 --> 11:47.260
the 1st Front Army is the troop of the Nanchang Uprising

227
11:47.260 --> 11:48.560
and the Autumn Harvest Uprising.

228
11:48.560 --> 11:50.310
It was led by Chairman Mao and Commander-in-Chief Zhu,

229
11:50.310 --> 11:52.240
so we should call you big brothers.

230
11:52.480 --> 11:53.050
Okay.

231
11:56.360 --> 11:58.170
How about I call you little big brother?

232
11:58.170 --> 11:58.780
How about that?

233
11:58.780 --> 11:59.980
You're really funny.

234
12:00.480 --> 12:04.600
Then I'll call you the 4th Front Army big brother.

235
12:04.740 --> 12:05.310
Okay.

236
12:05.560 --> 12:07.290
Thank you for the salt, 4th Big Brother.

237
12:07.290 --> 12:08.040
You're welcome.

238
12:08.040 --> 12:09.010
Little Big Brother.

239
12:09.010 --> 12:09.840
4th Big Brother.

240
12:09.840 --> 12:10.970
Little Big Brother.

241
12:12.020 --> 12:19.610
♪ Barefoot wading through the stream ♪

242
12:19.930 --> 12:23.410
♪ Fish swish their tails in wooden tubs ♪

243
12:23.410 --> 12:24.430
This song is really nice.

244
12:24.430 --> 12:25.830
The one singing is Ximei.

245
12:28.520 --> 12:30.480
Squad Leader, you can sing it too?

246
12:31.360 --> 12:32.960
What do you mean I can sing it?

247
12:32.960 --> 12:34.170
I was the one who taught Ximei

248
12:34.170 --> 12:35.270
to sing this song.

249
12:36.410 --> 12:37.410
My parents died

250
12:37.560 --> 12:38.750
when I was little.

251
12:38.910 --> 12:41.970
I carried her on my back and we begged for food together.

252
12:42.060 --> 12:43.610
Once, we went to Guangxi.

253
12:43.760 --> 12:46.070
We didn't get a single bite of food all day,

254
12:46.070 --> 12:47.930
and she cried loudly from hunger.

255
12:48.060 --> 12:50.320
I really couldn't think of any way to coax her,

256
12:50.320 --> 12:52.250
so I taught her to sing this song.

257
12:52.600 --> 12:54.430
As she sang, she wasn't hungry anymore.

258
12:54.430 --> 12:56.910
As she sang, she fell asleep on my back.

259
12:57.140 --> 12:58.610
As she kept singing,

260
12:59.760 --> 13:01.400
she grew up.

261
13:04.880 --> 13:09.240
[Maogong County, Sichuan; Catholic Church]

262
13:08.200 --> 13:09.200
Comrades!

263
13:09.310 --> 13:10.670
Comrades!

264
13:11.070 --> 13:12.710
Comrades, comrades!

265
13:12.930 --> 13:15.790
Welcome the Central Committee leaders to visit us!

266
13:15.890 --> 13:18.890
Great!

267
13:21.060 --> 13:22.260
Vice Chairman Zhou.

268
13:22.350 --> 13:23.320
Comrades.

269
13:23.590 --> 13:26.560
Please welcome Chairman Mao to the stage to speak to us!

270
13:26.560 --> 13:27.840
Great!

271
13:29.320 --> 13:30.370
I'll just speak here.

272
13:30.370 --> 13:31.570
I'll just speak here.

273
13:33.600 --> 13:34.440
Comrades,

274
13:34.580 --> 13:36.460
our 1st and 4th Front Armies

275
13:36.720 --> 13:38.650
have successfully joined forces!

276
13:38.720 --> 13:40.360
Great!

277
13:47.760 --> 13:50.470
In the history of our Red Army,

278
13:51.080 --> 13:53.800
this is a new record of invincibility.

279
13:53.850 --> 13:55.290
It shows that the Chinese Soviet

280
13:55.290 --> 13:56.690
has sufficient strength

281
13:56.690 --> 13:58.330
to defeat the Kuomintang reactionaries

282
13:58.330 --> 13:59.990
and complete the task of marching north

283
13:59.990 --> 14:01.370
to resist Japanese aggression.

284
14:01.370 --> 14:02.540
Great!

285
14:07.130 --> 14:07.930
Chairman Mao.

286
14:08.040 --> 14:09.500
Which one is Chairman Mao?

287
14:10.780 --> 14:12.640
Is this bearded man Chairman Mao?

288
14:14.480 --> 14:15.370
It's me.

289
14:15.450 --> 14:17.110
The one on the Kuomintang reactionaries' wanted list,

290
14:17.110 --> 14:19.710
with a bounty of 100,000 silver dollars, is me.

291
14:21.680 --> 14:23.340
The joining of the 2 front armies

292
14:23.340 --> 14:25.630
proves that our Red Army is invincible.

293
14:26.650 --> 14:27.680
Invincible.

294
14:27.930 --> 14:30.530
The 1st and 4th Front Armies are one family.

295
14:30.720 --> 14:32.770
We must learn from each other,

296
14:32.960 --> 14:33.840
unite well,

297
14:34.080 --> 14:35.200
and fight together

298
14:35.580 --> 14:36.560
to drive the Japanese imperialists

299
14:36.560 --> 14:37.620
out of our homeland

300
14:37.770 --> 14:40.010
and wipe out the Kuomintang reactionaries.

301
14:40.010 --> 14:41.660
100,000 silver dollars is not that easy to earn.

302
14:41.660 --> 14:43.790
We won't let them earn a single dollar.

303
14:44.960 --> 14:49.200
Great!

304
14:50.890 --> 14:52.040
Chairman, please sit.

305
14:52.040 --> 14:53.540
The performance will start shortly.

306
14:53.540 --> 14:54.540
Leaders, please.

307
15:06.770 --> 15:09.200
The get-together officially begins!

308
15:09.560 --> 15:10.890
Great!

309
15:11.980 --> 15:14.200
Now, let's welcome Comrade Li Bozhao and her colleagues from the Publicity Department

310
15:14.200 --> 15:16.800
of the General Political Department to the stage for their performance.

311
15:16.800 --> 15:18.200
Great!

312
15:28.410 --> 15:29.370
Comrades,

313
15:29.600 --> 15:31.160
our art troupe of the General Political Department

314
15:31.160 --> 15:35.480
[Li Bozhao, Staff Member of the Publicity Department of the Red Army's General Political Department]

315
15:31.530 --> 15:34.260
has gone through long-term combat and marching.

316
15:34.290 --> 15:35.690
We have lost some actors,

317
15:35.850 --> 15:37.370
and most of the props.

318
15:37.890 --> 15:38.800
So today's performance

319
15:38.800 --> 15:40.090
is not well-rehearsed.

320
15:40.090 --> 15:41.650
We hope for your understanding.

321
15:41.650 --> 15:43.130
That's okay!

322
15:44.360 --> 15:46.560
Now please enjoy the Soviet dance,

323
15:46.800 --> 15:48.010
"Sailor Dance".

324
15:49.010 --> 15:51.530
Great!

325
16:21.390 --> 16:23.550
Why is the leader's hair so long?

326
16:23.570 --> 16:25.650
That leader's beard is also quite long.

327
16:25.650 --> 16:27.270
Are they saying my beard is long

328
16:27.270 --> 16:28.550
or your hair is long?

329
16:31.060 --> 16:32.320
Isn't he the Chairman?

330
16:42.050 --> 16:44.410
Great!

331
16:44.450 --> 16:45.140
Great!

332
17:06.510 --> 17:08.700
Great!

333
17:16.680 --> 17:17.650
Next, please enjoy...

334
17:17.650 --> 17:18.609
Leader, urgent telegram.

335
17:18.609 --> 17:20.569
a song brought by the propaganda troupe

336
17:20.569 --> 17:21.720
of the Political Department of the 1st Red Army Corps.

337
17:21.720 --> 17:23.280
Great!

338
17:28.730 --> 17:29.720
A telegram from Zhang (Zhang Guotao) and Chen (Chen Changhao).

339
17:29.720 --> 17:30.520
Salute!

340
17:34.000 --> 17:35.130
Telegram from Zhang and Chen.

341
17:35.130 --> 17:36.860
There are unexpected changes.

342
17:36.930 --> 17:38.680
Today, we'll perform

343
17:38.760 --> 17:40.520
"The Song of the Reunion of the Two Main Forces,"

344
17:40.520 --> 17:42.390
written by Comrade Lu Dingyi, Director of the Publicity Department

345
17:42.390 --> 17:44.520
of the General Political Department.

346
17:44.850 --> 17:45.650
Ready!

347
17:45.760 --> 17:47.520
One, two, three, sing!

348
17:47.950 --> 17:56.320
♪ The two main forces have joined in the Qionglai Mountains ♪

349
17:57.040 --> 18:00.840
♪ Welcome the 4th Front Army♪

350
17:59.680 --> 18:00.650
Watch the show.

351
18:00.930 --> 18:05.240
♪ Our brave comrades, victorious in a hundred battles ♪

352
18:05.650 --> 18:09.280
♪ Unite the forces at the heart of China's Soviet movement ♪

353
18:09.930 --> 18:13.280
♪ Unite the forces at the heart of China's Soviet movement ♪

354
18:13.440 --> 18:17.610
♪ Resolutely turn all Sichuan red ♪

355
18:18.330 --> 18:25.930
♪ On the Long March, we braved the dangers of 8 provinces ♪

356
18:26.440 --> 18:29.760
♪ With iron will and blood sacrifice ♪

357
18:29.960 --> 18:34.440
♪ We achieved this great reunion ♪

358
18:34.760 --> 18:38.240
♪ To bring revolution to the people, lay a solid foundation for China ♪

359
18:38.760 --> 18:42.200
♪ To bring revolution to the people, lay a solid foundation for China ♪

360
18:42.330 --> 18:46.650
♪ Raise the red flag high and march forward ♪

361
18:46.960 --> 18:48.720
Great!

362
18:52.780 --> 18:53.690
One more.

363
18:53.720 --> 18:56.200
Good. One more.

364
19:06.480 --> 19:08.240
Next, I'll perform a piece

365
19:08.330 --> 19:10.810
of clapper marching tune.

366
19:16.330 --> 19:18.960
In March, we fought back to Guizhou Province,

367
19:18.960 --> 19:20.990
occupied Zunyi City for the second time,

368
19:20.990 --> 19:23.100
defeated Wang Jialie's 8 Regiments,

369
19:23.130 --> 19:25.890
and wiped out the troops of Xue and Wu's 2 Divisions.

370
19:25.890 --> 19:27.280
Great!

371
19:27.370 --> 19:28.720
That was a really good song!

372
19:28.720 --> 19:30.370
Since April, we marched south,

373
19:30.370 --> 19:31.960
fought at Guiyang and then Kunming,

374
19:31.960 --> 19:33.650
cleverly crossed the Jinsha River,

375
19:33.650 --> 19:36.130
and marched mightily in Sichuan.

376
19:36.240 --> 19:37.570
Great!

377
19:39.570 --> 19:41.340
In May, we captured Luding Bridge,

378
19:41.340 --> 19:43.380
sending the defenders fleeing,

379
19:43.410 --> 19:44.890
flew over the natural barrier Dadu River,

380
19:44.890 --> 19:46.890
and 17 warriors showed their heroism.

381
19:46.890 --> 19:48.280
In June, we crossed the snow mountains,

382
19:48.280 --> 19:49.810
tested on Jiajin Mountain,

383
19:49.850 --> 19:51.150
the 1st and 4th Front Armies,

384
19:51.150 --> 19:53.840
smiled happily when they met in Maogong.

385
19:54.170 --> 19:56.480
Great!

386
19:56.820 --> 20:03.200
Great!

387
20:10.040 --> 20:11.930
You are 4th Big Brother?

388
20:12.650 --> 20:14.380
You are the little big brother?

389
20:16.650 --> 20:18.110
When do you change shifts?

390
20:18.120 --> 20:19.610
I'll take you in to watch the performance.

391
20:19.610 --> 20:21.410
The comrades in our Squad all want to go in and watch,

392
20:21.410 --> 20:23.200
so I stood guard for them.

393
20:24.650 --> 20:25.700
Are they bullying you?

394
20:25.700 --> 20:27.460
No, I volunteered.

395
20:27.720 --> 20:28.870
I'm the oldest in our Squad.

396
20:28.870 --> 20:29.800
I'm already 20.

397
20:29.970 --> 20:30.860
They wanted to go in and watch the performance,

398
20:30.860 --> 20:31.810
so I let them in.

399
20:32.570 --> 20:33.970
Then Fourth Big Brother,

400
20:34.440 --> 20:36.970
do you want to go in and watch the performance?

401
20:38.040 --> 20:39.280
Of course I do.

402
20:39.450 --> 20:40.240
I am a propaganda troupe member

403
20:40.240 --> 20:41.610
of the Political Department of the 1st Corps.

404
20:41.610 --> 20:42.720
What song do you want to hear?

405
20:42.720 --> 20:43.850
I'll sing it for you.

406
20:47.000 --> 20:47.720
Really?

407
20:47.960 --> 20:48.890
Of course.

408
20:49.720 --> 20:52.330
Consider it a repayment for that bag of salt you gave me.

409
20:52.330 --> 20:52.930
Okay.

410
20:53.440 --> 20:54.440
I'm from Sichuan.

411
20:54.610 --> 20:56.610
I've never been to the Central Soviet Area.

412
20:56.610 --> 20:58.410
Just sing a song from the Central Soviet Area.

413
20:58.410 --> 20:58.960
Okay.

414
20:59.930 --> 21:01.660
Then I'll sing what I'm best at.

415
21:02.000 --> 21:02.680
Okay.

416
21:02.810 --> 21:03.680
Okay.

417
21:18.280 --> 21:20.650
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

418
21:20.850 --> 21:23.200
♪ Workers and peasants welcome us everywhere ♪

419
21:23.820 --> 21:26.140
♪ Officers and soldiers stand as equals ♪

420
21:26.440 --> 21:28.960
♪ No one oppresses anyone else ♪

421
21:29.280 --> 21:31.730
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

422
21:31.890 --> 21:34.130
♪ Workers and peasants unite to kill the enemy ♪

423
21:34.610 --> 21:37.200
♪ Compradors, gentry, and landlords ♪

424
21:37.200 --> 21:39.930
♪ We fight them without mercy ♪

425
21:40.140 --> 21:42.470
[Maogong, Sichuan]

426
21:40.240 --> 21:41.700
Zhang and Chen's telegram

427
21:41.850 --> 21:42.890
claims

428
21:42.470 --> 21:44.810
[Temporary Encampment of the Central Committee and the Central Military Commission]

429
21:43.410 --> 21:45.330
they support the Central Committee's plan to go north,

430
21:45.330 --> 21:48.060
but the content is all about going west and south.

431
21:48.370 --> 21:50.170
This is their roundabout tactic.

432
21:50.170 --> 21:52.810
Going west is passively avoiding battle,

433
21:52.960 --> 21:54.820
and going south is a risky attack.

434
21:54.890 --> 21:57.420
Both of these are the ideas we aimed to correct

435
21:57.610 --> 21:59.090
at the Zunyi Conference.

436
22:00.070 --> 22:03.830
They also said the 1st Front Army should attack Aba,

437
22:04.080 --> 22:07.140
and the 4th Front Army should turn back west of Songpan.

438
22:07.470 --> 22:10.130
Are we parting ways before even joining forces?

439
22:10.640 --> 22:11.640
This is nonsense.

440
22:11.890 --> 22:14.780
Could there be some misunderstanding?

441
22:15.130 --> 22:16.610
There's no misunderstanding.

442
22:16.610 --> 22:17.410
On June 13th,

443
22:17.440 --> 22:18.960
Zhang Guotao wrote an article

444
22:18.960 --> 22:19.930
titled

445
22:20.130 --> 22:21.930
"New Victory and New Situation".

446
22:21.930 --> 22:23.390
In it, he explicitly proposed

447
22:23.390 --> 22:25.520
developing towards the west or south.

448
22:26.850 --> 22:29.420
The national anti-Japanese upsurge is approaching.

449
22:29.420 --> 22:31.690
The overall revolutionary situation is heading north.

450
22:31.690 --> 22:32.990
The Central Committee's policy of going north

451
22:32.990 --> 22:34.720
to Sichuan, Shaanxi, and Gansu

452
22:35.440 --> 22:36.370
is beyond doubt.

453
22:40.650 --> 22:41.720
How about this?

454
22:42.770 --> 22:45.730
Let's invite Comrade Li Xiannian over

455
22:46.000 --> 22:48.130
to learn about the situation from him.

456
22:49.260 --> 22:50.660
Okay, I'll go invite him.

457
22:56.030 --> 22:56.560
Jin Biao.

458
22:57.000 --> 22:57.480
Here.

459
22:57.840 --> 22:59.040
Go invite Comrade Li Xiannian.

460
22:59.040 --> 22:59.570
Yes, sir.

461
23:20.890 --> 23:21.850
Report!

462
23:23.410 --> 23:24.470
Comrade Xiannian.

463
23:24.480 --> 23:25.010
Leaders.

464
23:25.060 --> 23:26.470
Come, Comrade Xiannian.

465
23:28.890 --> 23:30.300
Comrade Xiannian, sit here.

466
23:30.300 --> 23:32.300
Yes, Comrade Xiannian, take a seat.

467
23:34.280 --> 23:35.680
Comrade Xiannian, here.

468
23:36.890 --> 23:37.980
Have a bowl of hot milk tea first.

469
23:37.980 --> 23:39.110
Drink some milk tea.

470
23:44.930 --> 23:48.040
Leaders, what can I do for you?

471
23:49.040 --> 23:51.040
Don't be nervous.

472
23:51.680 --> 23:53.890
Comrade Xiannian, we invited you here

473
23:54.280 --> 23:55.680
to learn about

474
23:55.720 --> 23:58.240
the situation in the Min and Jialing Rivers areas,

475
23:58.240 --> 24:01.330
to see if we can still go north,

476
24:01.330 --> 24:03.370
fight back to the Sichuan-Shaanxi Soviet Area,

477
24:03.370 --> 24:06.330
or even develop towards Gansu.

478
24:12.440 --> 24:13.680
Leaders,

479
24:13.810 --> 24:15.090
regarding this matter,

480
24:15.090 --> 24:18.130
our Commander-in-Chief Xu Xiangqian once talked with me.

481
24:18.130 --> 24:19.280
We both believe

482
24:19.330 --> 24:22.720
that going north to Sichuan, Shaanxi, and Gansu is entirely possible.

483
24:22.720 --> 24:24.850
Comrade Xiannian, tell us your views.

484
24:24.960 --> 24:25.760
Okay.

485
24:26.760 --> 24:28.520
Commander-in-Chief Xu and I both believe that,

486
24:28.520 --> 24:30.340
given the support among the local population,

487
24:30.340 --> 24:31.080
the geographical conditions,

488
24:31.080 --> 24:33.410
and the Red Army's urgent need

489
24:33.440 --> 24:35.100
for rest and reinforcements,

490
24:35.230 --> 24:36.300
the two armies

491
24:36.570 --> 24:38.240
should advance north after joining forces.

492
24:38.240 --> 24:39.890
The most advantageous course would be

493
24:39.890 --> 24:41.810
to advance first into the area between the Min

494
24:41.810 --> 24:42.940
and Jialing Rivers.

495
24:51.000 --> 24:54.330
But I don't know if our view

496
24:54.650 --> 24:57.810
is right or wrong.

497
24:58.240 --> 25:00.370
Comrade Xiannian, what you just said,

498
25:00.650 --> 25:02.760
whether strategically or tactically,

499
25:02.760 --> 25:05.620
is consistent with the Central Committee's ideas.

500
25:06.650 --> 25:08.130
It seems that in the 4th Front Army,

501
25:08.130 --> 25:11.330
there are comrades who agree with the Central Committee.

502
25:11.480 --> 25:12.650
My thought is still

503
25:12.890 --> 25:14.650
to reply to Zhang and Chen again,

504
25:14.650 --> 25:17.000
reiterating the Central Committee's policy of going north,

505
25:17.000 --> 25:18.130
and to persuade them

506
25:18.170 --> 25:20.090
that whether advancing west or moving south,

507
25:20.090 --> 25:21.570
neither is a wise move,

508
25:22.240 --> 25:24.170
let alone a long-term strategy.

509
25:24.440 --> 25:25.960
Since Comrade Zhang Guotao

510
25:25.960 --> 25:28.520
published "New Victory and New Situation",

511
25:28.720 --> 25:30.330
I can also write an article

512
25:30.600 --> 25:32.930
to discuss the Central Committee's policy of marching north

513
25:32.930 --> 25:34.720
and its necessity and rationality,

514
25:34.720 --> 25:37.520
to unify everyone's thinking theoretically.

515
25:37.650 --> 25:38.330
I agree.

516
25:38.650 --> 25:40.040
Comrade Luofu's theory

517
25:40.170 --> 25:41.200
is second to none.

518
25:42.260 --> 25:42.740
Here.

519
25:44.960 --> 25:45.720
Okay.

520
25:48.760 --> 25:50.920
The CPC Central Committee and the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

521
25:50.920 --> 25:53.680
have consulted with Zhang Guotao by telegram several times,

522
25:53.680 --> 25:54.760
but still,

523
25:54.760 --> 25:57.240
no agreement has been reached on the strategic policy of marching north

524
25:57.240 --> 25:58.970
to Sichuan, Shaanxi and Gansu.

525
25:59.280 --> 26:00.810
The Central Committee decided

526
26:00.810 --> 26:03.270
that on June 26, 1935,

527
26:03.710 --> 26:06.300
an enlarged meeting of the Politburo would be held

528
26:03.990 --> 26:09.260
[Lianghekou, Maogong County, Sichuan]

529
26:06.450 --> 26:08.980
at Lianghekou, in the northern part of Maogong County,

530
26:08.980 --> 26:13.840
to jointly discuss the strategic course to be adopted after the 2 armies joined forces.

531
26:21.130 --> 26:21.780
Chairman,

532
26:22.040 --> 26:24.440
what kind of person is this Chairman Zhang?

533
26:26.390 --> 26:28.850
Chairman Zhang is an extraordinary figure.

534
26:29.330 --> 26:30.730
How is he extraordinary?

535
26:32.130 --> 26:33.960
He participated in the May Fourth Movement.

536
26:33.960 --> 26:36.010
He attended the First National Congress of the Party

537
26:36.010 --> 26:37.280
and the Nanchang Uprising.

538
26:37.280 --> 26:38.570
He has been to the Soviet Union.

539
26:38.570 --> 26:41.230
He served as a representative to the Comintern.

540
26:41.760 --> 26:42.760
He even met Lenin.

541
26:43.130 --> 26:45.000
Don't you think that's extraordinary?

542
26:45.000 --> 26:45.960
He met Lenin?

543
26:46.170 --> 26:47.440
That is truly extraordinary.

544
26:47.440 --> 26:48.040
Chairman.

545
26:48.200 --> 26:50.370
Did so many central leaders go to welcome him

546
26:50.370 --> 26:52.030
because he is extraordinary?

547
26:52.200 --> 26:53.170
Not entirely.

548
26:54.330 --> 26:55.730
It's for the sake of unity

549
26:56.090 --> 26:57.890
so we can head north to resist Japan as soon as possible.

550
26:57.890 --> 26:59.220
Is he easy to unite with?

551
27:01.440 --> 27:02.600
He has met Lenin.

552
27:03.130 --> 27:04.190
How could he not be?

553
27:13.740 --> 27:15.000
It's raining heavily.

554
27:16.330 --> 27:18.330
Mao, Mao, come in and take shelter.

555
27:18.360 --> 27:19.430
Come in and take shelter.

556
27:19.430 --> 27:20.490
Changfeng, hurry!

557
27:20.810 --> 27:22.890
The weather on this plateau changes so fast.

558
27:22.890 --> 27:24.750
It's completely unpredictable.

559
27:39.320 --> 27:40.410
Enlai.

560
27:46.910 --> 27:47.980
Comrade Zedong,

561
27:48.520 --> 27:50.520
you and Zhang Guotao

562
27:50.720 --> 27:52.450
are old acquaintances, right?

563
27:53.640 --> 27:54.490
I suppose so.

564
27:55.000 --> 27:57.440
We first met in 1919.

565
27:57.850 --> 27:58.580
At that time,

566
27:58.710 --> 28:01.410
Mr. Dazhao was the director of the Peking University Library,

567
28:01.410 --> 28:02.810
and I was a librarian.

568
28:02.930 --> 28:04.370
We were introduced to each other

569
28:04.370 --> 28:05.630
at Mr. Dazhao's house.

570
28:06.440 --> 28:08.240
But at that time, Comrade Guotao

571
28:08.240 --> 28:11.240
didn't seem to think much of a country bumpkin like me.

572
28:12.720 --> 28:15.480
The second time was at the 1st National Congress of the Party.

573
28:15.480 --> 28:16.930
He hosted, and I took notes.

574
28:16.930 --> 28:19.280
He was very warm and friendly to me.

575
28:19.480 --> 28:21.370
We had a great conversation.

576
28:21.730 --> 28:23.060
We met many times later,

577
28:23.200 --> 28:24.990
but after the failure of the Great Revolution,

578
28:24.990 --> 28:27.130
I returned to Hunan to organize the Autumn Harvest Uprising,

579
28:27.130 --> 28:28.720
and later went up to Jinggang Mountain.

580
28:28.720 --> 28:30.130
I never saw him again.

581
28:30.720 --> 28:32.610
I met him in Moscow.

582
28:32.850 --> 28:34.910
At that time, he and Comrade Wang Ming

583
28:35.130 --> 28:36.220
had some disagreements.

584
28:36.220 --> 28:36.930
I met him

585
28:37.170 --> 28:39.090
during the Nanchang Uprising.

586
28:39.110 --> 28:40.990
But we didn't interact much.

587
28:41.650 --> 28:43.370
He came to Nanchang then,

588
28:43.820 --> 28:46.520
saying he was conveying the instructions of the Comintern representative.

589
28:46.520 --> 28:48.650
He said the conditions weren't right yet

590
28:48.650 --> 28:50.810
and told us to put the uprising on hold for the time being.

591
28:50.810 --> 28:52.520
I even slammed the table at him.

592
28:52.520 --> 28:54.740
Fortunately, many comrades firmly opposed it,

593
28:54.740 --> 28:56.440
so he didn't stick to his own view.

594
28:56.440 --> 28:58.130
Today's Comrade Zhang Guotao,

595
28:58.130 --> 28:59.390
compared to that time,

596
28:59.610 --> 29:01.890
is probably different again.

597
29:09.950 --> 29:11.040
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

598
29:11.040 --> 29:12.130
[Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

599
29:12.850 --> 29:13.880
I need a nail.

600
29:22.890 --> 29:24.170
They are here!

601
29:24.960 --> 29:25.960
They are here!

602
29:29.330 --> 29:30.000
Let's go!

603
29:31.170 --> 29:31.950
Umbrella, umbrella.

604
29:31.950 --> 29:33.190
Chairman, umbrella!

605
29:33.220 --> 29:34.130
No need.

606
30:36.810 --> 30:39.010
Their horses are much taller than ours.

607
30:40.350 --> 30:42.130
Not only are their horses taller,

608
30:42.130 --> 30:43.530
their clothes are newer.

609
31:00.930 --> 31:02.460
And they are fatter than us.

610
31:07.090 --> 31:15.090
♪ The two main forces have joined in the Qionglai Mountains ♪

611
31:15.930 --> 31:19.650
♪ Welcome the 4th Front Army♪

612
31:19.780 --> 31:23.890
♪ Our brave comrades, victorious in a hundred battles ♪

613
31:52.410 --> 31:54.130
Sorry to keep you waiting, brothers.

614
31:54.130 --> 31:57.130
You came out in person to greet me in this pouring rain.

615
31:57.170 --> 31:59.570
I really don't deserve such an honor.

616
31:59.720 --> 32:00.670
Comrade Guotao,

617
32:01.000 --> 32:02.820
we have been looking forward to this.

618
32:02.820 --> 32:04.890
The family is finally reunited.

619
32:05.200 --> 32:07.720
Runzhi, it's been 8 years

620
32:07.930 --> 32:09.280
since we parted.

621
32:09.630 --> 32:10.960
We, the representatives

622
32:10.960 --> 32:12.480
who attended the 1st National Congress of the CPC together,

623
32:12.480 --> 32:13.810
finally meet again.

624
32:14.090 --> 32:16.160
Mr. Dong Biwu, who is also a representative of the 1st National Congress,

625
32:16.160 --> 32:17.200
is also in the army.

626
32:17.200 --> 32:18.680
You can see him this time.

627
32:18.760 --> 32:20.200
Good, that's great.

628
32:22.330 --> 32:24.520
Runzhi, you've lost weight.

629
32:25.810 --> 32:27.670
Thanks to Generalissimo Chiang.

630
32:27.680 --> 32:30.410
After a long journey, how could I not lose weight?

631
32:32.000 --> 32:32.890
Yujie (Zhu De),

632
32:33.200 --> 32:34.890
Yujie.

633
32:35.200 --> 32:37.090
It's been 8 years since we last saw each other, too.

634
32:37.090 --> 32:38.020
Long time no see.

635
32:38.130 --> 32:39.280
Comrade Guotao.

636
32:39.930 --> 32:41.480
Since we parted at Sanheba,

637
32:41.850 --> 32:43.200
we finally meet again.

638
32:45.720 --> 32:46.440
Luofu.

639
32:46.490 --> 32:48.130
Comrade Guotao, long time no see.

640
32:48.130 --> 32:48.810
Enlai!

641
32:49.570 --> 32:50.770
My two good brothers.

642
32:51.010 --> 32:52.650
It's been over 4 years since we last met, right?

643
32:52.650 --> 32:53.090
Yes.

644
32:53.370 --> 32:54.890
Comrade Amosov.

645
32:57.880 --> 32:59.330
We meet again.

646
32:59.610 --> 33:03.060
Congratulations on the successful joining of our 2 armies.

647
33:03.090 --> 33:04.520
Comrade Bogunov.

648
33:04.760 --> 33:08.760
You remind me of the days in Moscow.

649
33:09.000 --> 33:10.520
Congratulations on our joining forces.

650
33:10.520 --> 33:11.000
Good.

651
33:12.970 --> 33:14.280
Hello, Comrade Guotao.

652
33:14.280 --> 33:15.280
Comrade Bocheng.

653
33:15.440 --> 33:16.310
Long time no see.

654
33:16.310 --> 33:17.960
Yes, it's been too long.

655
33:18.430 --> 33:19.360
Comrade Guotao.

656
33:20.000 --> 33:21.260
My fellow countryman!

657
33:21.680 --> 33:22.590
Long time no see.

658
33:22.590 --> 33:23.480
Yes, yes.

659
33:23.730 --> 33:24.840
Comrade Amosov.

660
33:24.870 --> 33:26.600
-Jiaxiang. -How have you been?

661
33:27.930 --> 33:30.090
Other leaders call each other comrade.

662
33:30.090 --> 33:31.890
Why is he calling them brothers?

663
33:32.460 --> 33:34.130
Maybe because he met Lenin.

664
33:37.430 --> 33:38.240
Let's go.

665
33:39.200 --> 33:40.040
Comrade Guotao.

666
33:40.040 --> 33:42.170
It wasn't easy for us to meet this time.

667
33:43.090 --> 33:44.550
Look, it was just raining.

668
33:44.570 --> 33:46.480
But it stopped as soon as we met.

669
33:46.510 --> 33:48.110
Let's all go inside and talk.

670
33:48.850 --> 33:52.340
[Chengdu, Sichuan]

671
33:49.030 --> 33:51.200
The Nationalist Army's claim of preventing Zhu and Mao from fleeing west

672
33:51.200 --> 33:52.610
has been heard for years.

673
33:52.930 --> 33:54.960
Now Zhu and Mao have fled west after all,

674
33:54.960 --> 33:56.890
achieving their intended goal.

675
33:55.430 --> 33:56.170
[Liu Xiang, Kuomintang Commander-in-Chief of the Sichuan Campaign to Suppress the Communists]

676
33:56.170 --> 33:56.920
[and Chairman of the Sichuan Provincial Government]

677
33:57.020 --> 33:57.760
[Liu Wenhui, Commander-in-Chief of the Sichuan-Xikang Border Defense Army of the Kuomintang]

678
33:57.130 --> 33:58.720
During their westward flight,

679
33:57.760 --> 33:58.500
[and Commander of the 24th Army]

680
33:58.960 --> 34:00.720
the field headquarters repeatedly ordered

681
34:00.720 --> 34:03.330
strict prevention of their joining forces with Xu Xiangqian's troops.

682
34:03.330 --> 34:06.170
The words are still ringing in our ears and the ink is not yet dry,

683
34:06.170 --> 34:07.000
yet Zhu and Mao

684
34:07.000 --> 34:10.460
eventually joined forces with Xu Xiangqian and Zhang Guotao.

685
34:10.560 --> 34:11.560
However...

686
34:13.810 --> 34:14.469
Go on.

687
34:15.300 --> 34:15.830
Yes, sir.

688
34:17.480 --> 34:19.850
However, the 6 route armies of Sichuan

689
34:20.159 --> 34:22.820
could not block Xu's troops from fleeing south.

690
34:22.889 --> 34:26.330
Hundreds of thousands of elite troops from the central government and provinces

691
34:26.330 --> 34:28.730
could not intercept Zhu and Mao's westward flight.

692
34:28.730 --> 34:30.889
Though separated by treacherous rivers and mountains,

693
34:30.889 --> 34:32.080
despite supply shortages,

694
34:32.080 --> 34:33.409
the ravages of disease,

695
34:33.600 --> 34:35.159
and the bitter frost and snow,

696
34:35.159 --> 34:37.370
nothing can stop the Communist Army.

697
34:46.210 --> 34:47.560
According to a Nationalist military telegram,

698
34:47.560 --> 34:49.639
the concentrated enemy forces were to be wiped out.

699
34:49.639 --> 34:51.960
Now that the Communist Army has gathered,

700
34:51.960 --> 34:53.290
why not annihilate them?

701
34:53.290 --> 34:55.130
They cannot be defeated individually.

702
34:55.130 --> 34:56.730
Now that they have joined forces,

703
34:56.730 --> 34:58.210
talking again about annihilating their concentrated forces

704
34:58.210 --> 35:00.120
is really shameless boasting.

705
35:00.440 --> 35:01.430
Which newspaper is this?

706
35:01.430 --> 35:02.100
Who wrote the editorial?

707
35:02.100 --> 35:03.000
This must be strictly investigated.

708
35:03.000 --> 35:04.400
Which sentence is wrong?

709
35:05.930 --> 35:07.000
He Guoguang.

710
35:07.520 --> 35:08.120
Present.

711
35:08.250 --> 35:10.370
You're the director of the Sichuan Staff Regiment.

712
35:10.370 --> 35:11.630
Tell us your thoughts.

713
35:11.770 --> 35:13.500
Generalissimo, I believe that

714
35:13.690 --> 35:16.410
since Zhu, Mao, and Xu Xiangqian's troops have joined forces,

715
35:16.410 --> 35:18.600
they will definitely seek to establish a new base.

716
35:18.600 --> 35:19.770
Skip the obvious.

717
35:20.370 --> 35:22.730
Generalissimo, the top priority should be

718
35:22.730 --> 35:25.640
to order all armies and counties in Sichuan Province

719
35:25.640 --> 35:26.560
to fortify strongholds and deny the enemy supplies,

720
35:26.560 --> 35:29.160
extensively build fortresses and blockades,

721
35:29.370 --> 35:31.170
and besiege the Communist Army.

722
35:34.850 --> 35:35.730
Yuanjing.

723
35:36.690 --> 35:39.350
They couldn't be stopped in Fujian and Jiangxi,

724
35:39.440 --> 35:42.000
but they can be stopped in my Sichuan?

725
35:42.220 --> 35:43.050
Chairman Liu.

726
35:43.770 --> 35:46.000
I don't think you need to worry too much.

727
35:46.290 --> 35:47.200
After all, you're

728
35:47.200 --> 35:48.420
not Chen Bonan (Chen Jitang),

729
35:48.420 --> 35:50.010
and the Sichuan Army is not the Guangdong Army.

730
35:50.010 --> 35:50.450
Right?

731
35:50.770 --> 35:53.410
You would never go easy on the Communist Army.

732
35:55.850 --> 35:57.020
Naturally.

733
35:57.890 --> 35:59.090
Yuanjing, continue.

734
35:59.250 --> 35:59.890
Yes, sir.

735
36:00.520 --> 36:02.080
As long as we besiege the Communist Army

736
36:02.080 --> 36:04.370
in the barren land of northwestern Sichuan,

737
36:04.370 --> 36:07.290
making them limited by the terrain and unable to maneuver,

738
36:07.290 --> 36:08.600
coupled with insufficient supplies,

739
36:08.600 --> 36:10.080
they definitely won't last long.

740
36:10.080 --> 36:12.010
Going west or south will be futile.

741
36:12.160 --> 36:14.250
My only concern is still the northern line.

742
36:14.250 --> 36:15.120
Commander Hu Zongnan's

743
36:15.120 --> 36:16.690
elite main forces

744
36:16.690 --> 36:18.850
are still scattered across southern Gansu.

745
36:18.850 --> 36:20.780
It will take time to assemble them.

746
36:21.000 --> 36:23.080
If the Communist Army suddenly flees north at this time...

747
36:23.080 --> 36:24.480
Yuanjing, rest assured.

748
36:24.730 --> 36:26.600
I'll send a telegram to Shoushan (Hu Zongnan),

749
36:26.600 --> 36:27.330
telling him

750
36:27.560 --> 36:29.090
to assemble his main forces

751
36:29.440 --> 36:31.440
on the Pingwu-Songpan line

752
36:31.690 --> 36:34.490
to prevent the Communist Army from fleeing north.

753
36:34.930 --> 36:35.850
In this way,

754
36:35.970 --> 36:37.120
adding up all our troops,

755
36:37.120 --> 36:38.560
there will be more than 200 regiments.

756
36:38.560 --> 36:40.690
The Red Army will either be wiped out in battle or perish from being trapped.

757
36:40.690 --> 36:42.850
Formulate this idea of yours into a battle plan,

758
36:42.850 --> 36:43.600
distribute it,

759
36:43.600 --> 36:44.520
and strictly execute it.

760
36:44.520 --> 36:45.080
Yes, sir.

761
36:46.330 --> 36:49.530
Gentlemen, we believe in unity and sincere cooperation,

762
36:49.810 --> 36:51.070
but we don't do it well.

763
36:51.210 --> 36:52.930
The Red Army believes in unity, too.

764
36:52.930 --> 36:54.690
They do a better job of it than we do.

765
36:54.690 --> 36:55.530
Therefore,

766
36:55.640 --> 36:58.480
despite repeated encirclement campaigns, the Red Army has never been wiped out

767
36:58.480 --> 37:00.960
and has managed to escape time and again.

768
37:04.290 --> 37:06.510
Whether we can wipe out the previous shame this time

769
37:06.510 --> 37:07.720
depends on you all.

770
37:09.330 --> 37:10.440
Yes, sir!

771
37:25.860 --> 37:26.530
Thank you.

772
37:36.520 --> 37:37.210
Today,

773
37:37.690 --> 37:38.620
Comrade Guotao,

774
37:38.690 --> 37:40.620
you should try our cook's cooking.

775
37:41.560 --> 37:42.940
You call them cooks?

776
37:43.690 --> 37:45.550
We still call them kitchen hands.

777
37:45.600 --> 37:47.930
This is Comrade Bocheng's contribution.

778
37:48.250 --> 37:50.020
After he came back from the Soviet Union,

779
37:50.020 --> 37:52.350
he translated many military theory works

780
37:52.380 --> 37:53.940
and some training manuals.

781
37:54.000 --> 37:55.640
He also changed some of the terms

782
37:55.640 --> 37:57.580
to distinguish the Red Army from the old army.

783
37:57.580 --> 37:58.610
For example, kitchen hand

784
37:58.610 --> 38:00.080
was changed to cook.

785
38:00.560 --> 38:02.520
Groom was changed to breeder.

786
38:02.640 --> 38:04.770
And orderly was changed to messenger.

787
38:04.930 --> 38:06.250
The term guerrilla warfare

788
38:06.250 --> 38:08.640
was also translated and named by Comrade Bocheng,

789
38:08.640 --> 38:09.210
right?

790
38:10.850 --> 38:12.310
What was it called before?

791
38:12.890 --> 38:13.690
This tactic,

792
38:13.710 --> 38:16.090
in Western military terminology,

793
38:16.120 --> 38:17.890
originated from Spanish.

794
38:18.080 --> 38:18.890
Many times,

795
38:18.890 --> 38:21.020
it was translated as chimpanzee warfare.

796
38:21.020 --> 38:23.160
Actually, it's not translated correctly.

797
38:23.160 --> 38:24.230
As for chimpanzees,

798
38:24.230 --> 38:25.770
I thought at that time, in China,

799
38:25.770 --> 38:27.040
there were no such things at all.

800
38:27.040 --> 38:28.900
How could the commanders and fighters understand it?

801
38:28.900 --> 38:30.290
I remembered what was recorded in "Records of the Grand Historian",

802
38:30.290 --> 38:32.730
that Li Guang was good at attacking with light cavalry.

803
38:32.730 --> 38:33.850
I felt the meaning was similar,

804
38:33.850 --> 38:35.460
so I simply translated it as guerrilla warfare.

805
38:35.460 --> 38:36.060
Awesome.

806
38:36.810 --> 38:37.740
Really awesome.

807
38:39.010 --> 38:40.040
Speaking of guerrilla warfare,

808
38:40.040 --> 38:42.480
you, Mao Zedong, are famous for it.

809
38:44.530 --> 38:45.440
However,

810
38:46.080 --> 38:48.760
Xu Xiangqian of our 4th Front Army

811
38:48.980 --> 38:51.110
is also a master of guerrilla warfare.

812
38:51.810 --> 38:52.890
I know this.

813
38:53.040 --> 38:55.770
I have read his "Resolution on Military Issues".

814
38:55.850 --> 38:58.220
The 7 principles he proposed for guerrilla warfare

815
38:58.220 --> 39:00.290
are similar to our 16-character formula

816
39:00.290 --> 39:01.620
for guerrilla warfare.

817
39:02.560 --> 39:03.910
Come, Comrade Guotao, sit down.

818
39:03.910 --> 39:04.960
Come, Comrade Kai Feng.

819
39:04.960 --> 39:05.440
Runzhi.

820
39:05.440 --> 39:07.300
I find your memory is really good.

821
39:07.410 --> 39:10.090
It's been a few years since he wrote this article.

822
39:10.090 --> 39:11.370
Because it left a deep impression,

823
39:11.370 --> 39:12.640
I remember it firmly.

824
39:12.850 --> 39:14.310
Xiangqian is now in Lifan.

825
39:14.330 --> 39:15.690
When you meet,

826
39:16.040 --> 39:17.520
you can have a good discussion.

827
39:17.520 --> 39:19.410
And we will be here

828
39:19.620 --> 39:21.850
to create a new situation in Sichuan and Xikang.

829
39:21.850 --> 39:25.290
So we can still wage guerrilla warfare.

830
39:25.960 --> 39:26.890
Comrade Guotao,

831
39:27.040 --> 39:28.310
we have repeatedly talked about this issue

832
39:28.310 --> 39:29.990
in the telegrams before.

833
39:30.330 --> 39:30.850
Your point of view

834
39:30.850 --> 39:32.600
is now contrary to our Central Committee's strategy

835
39:32.600 --> 39:34.210
of going north.

836
39:34.760 --> 39:35.950
Don't be so sharp.

837
39:36.750 --> 39:38.690
Today, I read Comrade Luofu's article

838
39:38.690 --> 39:40.690
in the "Forward" newspaper,

839
39:40.810 --> 39:44.610
titled "Capture Songpan and Turn Sichuan, Shaanxi, and Gansu Red."

840
39:45.080 --> 39:45.930
It said that

841
39:46.120 --> 39:48.380
refusing to march north was opportunism

842
39:48.570 --> 39:50.620
and a tendency toward escapism.

843
39:51.440 --> 39:52.440
Comrade Luofu,

844
39:53.120 --> 39:55.580
you almost pointed at my nose and scolded me.

845
39:56.250 --> 40:00.520
Comrade Guotao, I'm just telling it like it is.

846
40:01.040 --> 40:03.560
Specific situations need specific analysis.

847
40:03.560 --> 40:04.730
What else is there to analyze?

848
40:04.730 --> 40:05.560
Your line

849
40:05.580 --> 40:07.290
is like a sparrow falling into a gutter.

850
40:07.290 --> 40:08.560
It can get in but can't get out.

851
40:08.560 --> 40:09.960
It's an obvious dead end.

852
40:12.250 --> 40:13.710
Don't be so angry,

853
40:13.740 --> 40:14.570
Comrade Bo Gu.

854
40:14.770 --> 40:16.540
I'm just putting forward my ideas

855
40:16.540 --> 40:17.940
for everyone to discuss.

856
40:18.250 --> 40:19.180
That's perfect.

857
40:19.250 --> 40:20.370
Then tell us,

858
40:20.980 --> 40:21.780
what's the deal with the

859
40:21.710 --> 40:24.420
[Kai Feng (He Kequan), Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee]

860
40:21.810 --> 40:23.870
Soviet Northwest Federal Government

861
40:23.870 --> 40:25.080
you just established?

862
40:25.080 --> 40:27.550
Who is this federation supposed to unite with?

863
40:27.550 --> 40:28.880
The Central Committee?

864
40:33.080 --> 40:34.160
Comrade Kai Feng.

865
40:35.160 --> 40:36.980
I find that this young fellow of mine speaks

866
40:36.980 --> 40:38.690
even more aggressively than Comrade Bo Gu.

867
40:38.690 --> 40:40.090
It suddenly reminds me of

868
40:40.160 --> 40:41.520
the time in Moscow

869
40:41.690 --> 40:42.910
during the Sixth Congress.

870
40:42.910 --> 40:44.860
Comrade Bo Gu's tone when translating

871
40:44.860 --> 40:46.530
was also this fierce.

872
40:47.480 --> 40:48.730
But Runzhi.

873
40:48.930 --> 40:50.160
We are here to join forces,

874
40:50.160 --> 40:51.970
not to argue, right?

875
40:52.000 --> 40:52.690
Right.

876
40:53.160 --> 40:55.850
Comrades Bo Gu and Kai Feng are outspoken,

877
40:55.930 --> 40:57.370
but we still need to unite.

878
40:57.370 --> 40:59.000
Speak more amiably.

879
40:59.120 --> 41:00.980
Arguing won't solve the problem.

880
41:01.580 --> 41:02.210
Chairman.

881
41:07.170 --> 41:08.040
There are 2 chairmen here.

882
41:08.040 --> 41:09.500
Which one are you calling?

883
41:11.250 --> 41:12.930
You should say "Chairmen."

884
41:14.640 --> 41:15.600
Come on, Chairman Zhang,

885
41:15.600 --> 41:17.260
try this fried chili peppers.

886
41:17.520 --> 41:20.080
This is our cook's specialty.

887
41:20.220 --> 41:21.300
Try it.

888
41:25.060 --> 41:26.310
Okay, I'll try it.

889
41:30.120 --> 41:31.120
Everyone, try it.

890
41:32.040 --> 41:33.640
Spicy, but delicious.

891
41:33.850 --> 41:34.780
It is delicious.

892
41:35.980 --> 41:37.240
If you don't eat chili,

893
41:37.810 --> 41:39.210
you're not a revolutionary.

894
41:39.210 --> 41:40.210
Comrade Zedong.

895
41:40.480 --> 41:41.850
There you go again.

896
41:42.140 --> 41:43.560
Whether one eats chili or not is just

897
41:43.560 --> 41:45.120
a personal dietary habit.

898
41:45.290 --> 41:47.220
Revolution is about party spirit,

899
41:47.250 --> 41:48.400
not about eating chili.

900
41:48.400 --> 41:48.920
Look.

901
41:49.020 --> 41:51.550
Comrade Bo Gu's words are spicier than chili.

902
41:53.160 --> 41:54.730
Are you going to eat it or not?

903
41:54.730 --> 41:56.590
For the revolution, I'll eat one.

904
42:13.520 --> 42:14.210
Yujie.

905
42:15.890 --> 42:17.290
Comrade Guotao, come.

906
42:17.570 --> 42:18.560
I hope I'm not disturbing your rest.

907
42:18.560 --> 42:19.330
No.

908
42:19.600 --> 42:20.600
Come, please sit.

909
42:20.690 --> 42:22.020
I heard your back hurts,

910
42:22.440 --> 42:25.100
especially after crossing the snow mountains.

911
42:25.330 --> 42:25.950
I happen to have

912
42:25.950 --> 42:28.150
some pain-relief plasters right here.

913
42:28.690 --> 42:30.080
I've used them, and they work well.

914
42:30.080 --> 42:31.210
I'll bring them for you.

915
42:31.210 --> 42:33.850
Thanks for your concern about my minor ailment.

916
42:33.850 --> 42:35.810
How can this be a minor ailment?

917
42:36.160 --> 42:38.120
You are the Commander-in-Chief of the whole army.

918
42:38.120 --> 42:40.850
Can the Commander-in-Chief's matters be minor?

919
42:42.230 --> 42:43.020
Come on.

920
42:44.770 --> 42:46.630
Thank you, Commander-in-Chief.

921
42:49.850 --> 42:50.730
Give it to me.

922
42:52.730 --> 42:53.930
There's a proper way

923
42:54.160 --> 42:56.040
to heat this plaster.

924
42:59.410 --> 43:00.600
Let the guard do it.

925
43:01.000 --> 43:01.850
No need.

926
43:02.290 --> 43:03.330
They don't know how.

927
43:03.330 --> 43:03.920
I'll do it.
